1.1.text:
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
THE REGENT OF EAST KOTAWARINGIN,
Considering : a. that every citizen has the right to security and freedom from all forms of violence against women and children which constitutes a violation of human rights, therefore their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination;
b. that violence against women and children in the region continues to increase, therefore protection efforts are required;
c. that laws and regulations governing the protection of women and children victims of violence have not yet regulated protection efforts at the regional level, therefore institutional support and regulations are needed to ensure their implementation;
d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a, b and c above, it is necessary to regulate and stipulate by Regional Regulation of East Kotawaringin Regency concerning the Implementation of Protection for Women and Children Victims of Violence.
In view of : 1. Law Number 27 of 1959 concerning the Stipulation of Emergency Law Number 3 of 1953 concerning the Establishment of Level II Regions in Kalimantan (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1953 Number 9, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 352) as Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1959 Number 72, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia 1820);
2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
3886);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
5606);
4. Law Number 13 of 2003 concerning Manpower (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 39, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4279);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number
4419);
6. Law Number 13 of 2006 concerning Protection of Witnesses and Victims (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635);
7. Law Number 21 of 2007 concerning the Eradication of the Criminal Act of Trafficking in Persons (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4720);
8. Law Number 11 of 2009 concerning Social Welfare (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2009 Number 12, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4976);
9. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
10.Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
11.Government Regulation Number 38 of 2007 concerning the Division of Government Affairs between the Government, Provincial Regional Government and Regency/Municipal Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 82, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4737);
12.Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection of the Republic of Indonesia Number 01 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards (SPM) in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 56);
13.Regional Regulation of East Kotawaringin Regency Number 6 of 2008 concerning Regional Government Affairs Which Are the Authority of the East Kotawaringin Regency Government (Regional Gazette of East Kotawaringin Regency Year 2008 Number 97).

Article 18
The community and family have the following obligations and responsibilities:
a. Prevent the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. Report if violence occurs;
c. Protect victims; and
d. Provide emergency assistance.

CHAPTER III
VIOLENCE
Article 5
Forms of violence include:
a. Physical violence;
b. Psychological violence;
c. Sexual violence;
d. Neglect;
e. Exploitation; and/or
f. other forms of violence.

Article 28
(1) Efforts to prevent violence against women and children shall be carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by the agency having the principal tasks and functions of coordination in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by:
a. Establishing a network in efforts to prevent violence;
b. Conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. Establishing a violence prevention system;
d. Conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
e. Providing critical education on the rights of women and children for the community.
f. Imposing a curfew for children which shall be further regulated by the Regent Regulation of East Kotawaringin.

Article 8
Sexual violence as referred to in Article 5 letter (c) consists of:
a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. forced sexual intercourse;
c. forced sexual intercourse in an unnatural or unwanted manner; and/or
d. forced sexual intercourse with another person for commercial purposes and/or specific purposes.

Article 13
Child victims of violence, in addition to obtaining the rights as referred to in Article 12, also obtain special rights, as follows:
a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to obtain proper education;
d. the right to equal protection;
e. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or
f. the right to obtain freedom in accordance with applicable norms.

Article 14
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement victim protection efforts, in the form of:
a. Establishing policies;
b. Forming FKPKK;
c. Preparing program and activity planning;
d. Providing facilities and infrastructure support;
e. Allocating budget; and
f. conducting guidance and supervision of the protection of women and children through related agencies.
(2) In the implementation of the obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall prepare a Regional Action Plan for victim protection.

